# SDM: FINCSTP/FDECSTP move TOP and "do not affect the tag word or the contents
# of any register." One push from empty puts the value in PHYSICAL R7, so the
# tag word is 0x3FFF no matter where TOP is afterwards.
INC1  0x3fff
DEC1  0x3fff
# CONTROL: TOP returns to its starting point. Box64 passes this because its two
# per-instruction errors cancel — which is why the case is here. Without it the
# other three read as "TOP handling is broken", a broader claim than the evidence
# supports.
RT1   0x3fff
# Seven pushes leave R1..R7 in use; FINCSTP must not change that.
IN7   0x0003
